  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia&apos;s APEC Support Program (AASP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Consistent with APEC&#x2019;s mission and guided by Australia&#x2019;s APEC priorities, Australia&#x2019;s APEC Support Program (AASP), provides technical cooperation and targeted capacity-building support to APEC developing economies to enhance their capacities to adopt and implement growth-generating economic and trade policies. It aims to promote rules-based trade, trade and investment liberalisation, structural reform, economic cooperation and regional prosperity across the APEC region, in line with Australia&apos;s long-term priorities. This includes support to the APEC Secretariat&apos;s Project Management Unit; contributions to the APEC Policy Support Unit; funding contributions to APEC&apos;s centralised project funding pool (the APEC Support Fund); and support for a range of targeted interventions led by DFAT, other Australian government agencies and selected partners.</narrative>
  </description>
